However, before I realized, there was an oddly mellow\nwoman sitting next to my depressed, misanthropic, and\nintroverted self.%K%P
然后，当我注意到时，\n在那如此阴郁、别扭、畏缩的我身旁，\n已经坐着一位优雅谦和的女性了。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
We met on a tennis club's sightseeing trip -- hardly a\nremarkable location, all things considered -- and after\nspending some time talking, began dating with no drama or\nanything.%K%P
那是网球部集训合宿的时候，\n在常见到不能再常见，甚至连印象都没留下的地方我遇见了她。\n毫无戏剧性，我们只是普通地说了话，然后开始交往了。%K%P
She was neither particularly forceful, nor as hopelessly\nintroverted as me.%K%P
她非常非常积极，\n和消极的我完全不同。%K%P
Then again, her behavior wasn't really based on some\nirreversible set of values, and she kept being overwhelmed\nand lead by other people, never able to refuse an\ninvitation or a favor.%K%P
但是，她也不是那种基于自己坚定的信念而行动的人，\n很容易随波逐浪，不太会拒绝。%K%P
She got together with me simply because she felt a certain\nsense of kinship. Being completely oblivious to her own\npopularity, she eventually began attending university from\nmy room, and...%K%P
只是以彼此『合得来』这样的理由，\n不顾众多追求者的目光，\n和我手挽着手从房间出来，一同走向大学教室…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAsami promised to teach me the happiness of being a\nfamily, having children, and working for someone else's\nsake -- a future filled with joy.\d%K%P
「麻实她说过要向我呈现的。\n呈现构筑家庭，爱着自己的孩子，为了家庭而工作的幸福。\n呈现被那样的开心快乐所包裹的未来」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI... see.\d%K%P
「这样…啊」%K%P
That was why she urged me not to be scared... that I could\ntake her as my wife \dwithout overthinking things.\d%K%P
所以她才会对我说结婚没什么可怕的。\n说『放心吧，我会嫁给你的』%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dDid you... love her?\d%K%P
「当时…你喜欢老师么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI did. It's not something I actually said out loud all\nthat often, but it's how I've always felt deep down in my\nheart.\d%K%P
「我爱她。\n口头上表达不出来的部分，一直留存在心里」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut... I think it was precisely this lack of decisiveness\nthat ended up being the root of everything that came\nafter.\d%K%P
「但是啊…到最后，\n我都没能做到身为男人应该有的主动与坦率，\n从开始就是，一切结局都是必然，一切梦想都是空谈。」%K%P
If I had been the one who proposed to Asami...%K%P
如果当初是由我向麻实求婚的话…%K%P
If I only tried to earn my own happiness... if I only\ndecided and acted for myself...%K%P
通过自己的努力获得幸福，\n靠着自己去思考、去行动的话…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dFor the whole time we were living together, I was unable\nto become truly responsible for the both of us.\d%K%P
「在我们两个人一起生活的期间，\n我一直没能承担起两人份的责任」%K%P
Having children or buying a house were empty promises. I\nburied myself in my job and treated Asami the exact same\nway I did during our university years.%K%P
要生孩子，要盖一栋独门独院的大房子，\n这些约定真的都是黄粱美梦啊…\n我漫无目标地努力工作，努力用自己的想法去爱麻实。%K%P
We were happy, with no pressing concerns to think of\nduring our unchanging everyday lives. As a result, time\nsimply went on without me having to make a single\ndecision.%K%P
现状的幸福让我对一成不变的生活感到了满足，\n于是我什么也不想，就这么一天天地过下去。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dShe simply couldn't put up with that...\nWell, I guess it's too late to cry about it now.\d%K%P
「后来她大概是无法忍受那样的生活了…\n哎，现在才注意到也已经晚了」%K%P
I left all the important decisions to someone else.%K%P
在做重要决定的时候，我总是寄希望于别人。%K%P
So with only the two of us in the relationship, I ended up\nbeing a coward who shied away from all decisions, and she\na miserable woman burdened with all the tough choices.%K%P
也就是说，这两个人就是\n总把最终决定权交给别人的懦弱的男人，\n和总是为艰难决定苦恼的不幸的女人。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIn the end, I even forced her to file for the divorce.\nNow that I say it out loud, it really hits me how much of\na bastard I was.\d%K%P
「到最后，连分手的话也都是麻实来说的…\n啊～，从嘴里说出来我终于懂了啊。\n我实在是无药可救，差劲至极」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...No.\d%K%P
「………别这么说」%K%P
Toko slowly raised her head from the picture.%K%P
一直盯着我和麻实照片的都子，\n慢慢把头抬了起来。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThat's not true.\d%K%P
「那样的事情，才没有…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
Her youthful features seemed to have disappeared behind\nthe mask of some complex and unstable emotion, her eyes\ntaking on a passionate light, making me slightly\nuncomfortable.%K%P
跟平常稚嫩的脸庞不同，\n眼睛有点润湿，脸上流露出不安的情绪，\n看着她这个样子，我也没法镇定下来了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou're always doing your best, Osamu.\nI can guarantee that you're not a bastard!\d%K%P
「理君，总是很努力啊。\n绝对不是什么渣男…我保证」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dTh-Thanks...\d%K%P
「谢、谢谢…」%K%P
Her somewhat nasal, unsteady voice, completely different\nfrom her usual cheerful tone, made my heart race a little.%K%P
跟平常精神满满的发言不同，\n稍微带点鼻音。这被不安的感情充满的声音\n触碰到了我的脸颊，让我心跳不止。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dEven if you were the wrong man for Ms. Kouno, it doesn't\nmean you would be wrong for me.\d%K%P
「即使对老师而言理君是糟糕的男人…\n但对我而言可未必是那样的啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut I was a terrible husband for Asami.\nThat's just a fact.\d%K%P
「可我确实是麻实最差劲的丈夫。\n只有这一点，是不会错的，过去也已经证明了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThat has nothing to do with me!\d%K%P
「那个跟我又没有关系」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
Her passionate eyes; her mouth, heaving hot breaths...%K%P
那润湿的眼睛，吐着微热气息的小嘴…%K%P
...pressed against my shoulder, momentarily taking me\naback.%K%P
她按住我的肩膀，不住地摇着头。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou have me...!\nAnd I'll never give up on you!\d%K%P
「理君你…还有我啊。\n我一定不会抛弃你的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dToko...\d%K%P
「都子…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSo, Osamu... let's be happy together, okay?\d%K%P
「所以理君…一定要幸福起来哦」%K%P
It wasn't... my wife standing in front of me.%K%P
此刻在我身边的，并不是我深爱的妻子。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI won't say that we should seek happiness together like\nMs. Kouno did, but...\d%K%P
「不过像老师那样，两个人一起为幸福而努力什么的，\n我没法那么说」%K%P
But it was still a person I loved deeply, that much was\ntrue.%K%P
只是有一件事情，我至今依然坚信着。\n那个人，一直都是我深爱的人，无论过去，还是现在。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI want my happiness to be your happiness.\d%K%P
「如果我得到幸福，\n同时也能让理君幸福起来的话，那就太好了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat... sounds like a very happy future.\d%K%P
「那还真是…非常幸福的愿景啊」%K%P
Or rather, she was actually -the- most important person in\nmy life right now.%K%P
不仅如此，那种愿景也是我而今存在的最大意义。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSo you don't need to torture yourself over things like\nthat.\nLet's cheer up together, okay?\d%K%P
「所以怎么可以为了那种事而消沉呢？\n打起精神来吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYeah... you're right... Thanks, Toko.\d%K%P
「嗯，嗯…\n谢谢你，都子」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dNo problem...!\d%K%P
「嗯…诶」%K%P
I wrapped my arms around Toko and patted her on the head,\nsqueezing her tighter in my embrace.%K%P
我伸出手臂，环抱住都子的肩，\n将她小小的脑袋置于胸前，轻轻抚摸着。%K%P
Her body was small and delicate, smelling like sweet\nmilk... and wriggling in my embrace like a cute, tiny\nanimal.%K%P
这个身体无论什么时候抱一下都感觉很娇嫩，\n散发着像牛奶般让人舒适的甜甜香味，\n而且微微的颤动让人觉得可爱极了。%K%P
As such, the pleasant tickling sensation of hot breath as\nshe parted her lips in my embrace completely diverted my\nattention from the words she uttered.%K%P
所以，贴在我胸前的嘴唇缓缓开合，\n只是吐出的气息就让我觉得难为情，\n能感觉到的除了阵阵舒适，还是阵阵舒适。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhy are you doing this again, Ms. Kouno...?\nWhy do you keep confusing him all the time like this?\d%K%P
「老师好过分…\n为什么总是一次次地让理君这么困扰…」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
